wt
------------------------------------------
Wt (pronounced witty) is a C++ library and application server for developing
and deploying web applications.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libGL1-23.3.6-1
  libGLEW2.1-2.1.0-1
  libGraphicsMagick3-1.3.49-1
  libX11_6-1.8.13-1
  libboost_filesystem1.66-1.66.0-1
  libboost_program_options1.66-1.66.0-1
  libboost_system1.66-1.66.0-1
  libboost_thread1.66-1.66.0-1
  libfcgi0-2.4.0-3
  libfontconfig1-2.18.3-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libglib2.0_0-2.90.1-1
  libhpdf2.4-2.4.6-1bl2
  libmariadb3-3.3.19-1
  libpango1.0_0-1.58.2-1
  libpq5-18.7-1
  libssl3-3.5.9-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  libwt4-4.15.0-1bl1
  zlib0-1.4-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libGL-devel-23.3.6-1
  libGLEW-devel-2.1.0-1
  libGraphicsMagick-devel-1.3.49-1
  libX11-devel-1.8.13-1
  libboost-devel-1.66.0-1
  libfcgi-devel-2.4.0-3
  libhpdf-devel-2.4.6-1bl2
  libmariadb-devel-3.3.19-1
  libpango1.0-devel-1.58.2-1
  libpng-devel-1.6.59-1
  libpq-devel-18.7-1
  libpq5-18.7-1
  libsqlite3-devel-3.49.1-1
  libssl-devel-3.5.9-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1
  zlib-devel-1.4-1

Canonical website:
  https://www.webtoolkit.eu/wt

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/emweb/wt/archive/refs/tags/4.15.0.tar.gz#/wt-4.15.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack wt-4.15.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./wt-4.15.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/wt-4.15.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/wt-4.15.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libwt4-4.15.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libwt-devel-4.15.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

